      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_76df7c7b",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: run_along_now_felicia; hasOverallIntent: Abusive; overall-intent-description: The image features a black-and-white photo of Marilyn Monroe waving, overlaid with text that reads 'run along now felicia' and 'you don't want to miss the water truck.....ya thirsty bitch.' The text is directed at a person named Felicia and uses a demeaning, threatening tone, implying she is desperate or in need of water, which can be interpreted as an abusive message. The use of the term 'thirsty bitch' is derogatory and potentially harmful, suggesting she is morally or physically deficient. The meme's intent is to harass or intimidate the individual named Felicia, fitting the definition of an abusive meme.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
